## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a dynamic string structure supporting weighted, prefix-based queries and order-statistics. A Trie augmented with per-node aggregates enables efficient prefix sums and k-th retrieval while handling duplicates via cumulative weights.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node aggregates (subtreeWeight, terminalWeight)
- O(len(word)) time complexity for insert/erase operations
- O(len(prefix)) for prefix-sum queries
- O(len(prefix) + len(target_word)) for kth-word queries
- Duplicate handling via cumulative weight values

## Code Example
```javascript
class WeightedTrie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  insertWord(word, w) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const idx = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[idx]) node.children[idx] = new TrieNode();
      node = node.children[idx];
      node.subtreeWeight += w;
    }
    node.terminalWeight += w;
  }

  eraseWord(word, w) {
    this.insertWord(word, -w);
  }

  queryPrefixSum(prefix) {
    let node = this.traverse(prefix);
    return node ? node.subtreeWeight : 0;
  }

  kthWordWithPrefix(prefix, k) {
    let node = this.traverse(prefix);
    if (!node || node.subtreeWeight < k) return null;
    let word = prefix;
    while (!node.terminalWeight) {
      for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
        if (!node.children[i]) continue;
        if (node.children[i].subtreeWeight >= k) {
          word += String.fromCharCode(97 + i);
          node = node.children[i];
          break;
        }
        k -= node.children[i].subtreeWeight;
      }
    }
    return word;
  }

  traverse(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      const idx = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[idx]) return null;
      node = node.children[idx];
    }
    return node;
  }
}

class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Array(26).fill(null);
    this.subtreeWeight = 0;
    this.terminalWeight = 0;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle concurrent updates to the Trie?
- How would you optimize memory usage for sparse tries?
- Can this be adapted for case-insensitive searches or Unicode characters?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data structure design for a common gaming feature, balancing efficient updates with query performance.

## Key Concepts
- Hash maps provide O(1) player score lookups
- Ordered maps enable range and top-k access
- Ordered sets handle duplicate scores within groups
- Rank computation accounts for tied scores

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating approach
class Leaderboard {
  constructor(){
    this.playerToScore = new Map();
    this.scoreToPlayers = new Map(); // descending keys; each maps to a Set of players
  }
  addOrUpdate(playerId, score) {
    // Remove from old score group if exists
    const oldScore = this.playerToScore.get(playerId);
    if (oldScore !== undefined) {
      const oldSet = this.scoreToPlayers.get(oldScore);
      oldSet.delete(playerId);
      if (oldSet.size === 0) this.scoreToPlayers.delete(oldScore);
    }
    // Update maps and add to new score group
    this.playerToScore.set(playerId, score);
    if (!this.scoreToPlayers.has(score)) {
      this.scoreToPlayers.set(score, new Set());
    }
    this.scoreToPlayers.get(score).add(playerId);
  }
}
```

